 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Local Minima:** The low dimensionality of $SO(3)$ induces local minima [S1]. The modulo loss mitigates this by making the loss landscape more convex [S1].
-*   **Unknown Translation:** If both object-to-camera distances and in-plane translations are unknown, the latent space becomes $SE(3)$ [S1]. MELON fails to jointly infer rotation $R_i$ and translation $T_i$ in this setup [S1].
-*   **Symmetry Matching:** If $N$ does not match the object's symmetry, convergence may be poor [S1]. The fractional covering $D_R(f^*)$ indicates the likelihood of convergence [S1].
+*   **Local Minima:** The low dimensionality of $SO(3)$ induces local minima. The modulo loss mitigates this by making the loss landscape more convex [S1].
+*   **Unknown Translation:** If both object-to-camera distances and in-plane translations are unknown, the latent space becomes $SE(3)$. MELON fails to jointly infer rotation $R_i$ and translation $T_i$ in this setup [S1].
+*   **Symmetry Matching:** If $N$ does not match the object's symmetry, convergence may be poor. The fractional covering $D_R(f^*)$ indicates the likelihood of convergence [S1].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Compute time per gradient step increases linearly with the replication order $N$ [S1]. For $N=1$, it takes 23 ms/it; $N=2$ takes 34 ms/it; $N=3$ takes 43 ms/it; $N=4$ takes 52 ms/it [S1].
